    <statement><p>Find the speed at the given value of t:</p>
<p><m>{\bf r\it(t)} = \left\lt e^{t-3},-11,3 t^{-1}\right&gt; , t=3</m></p>
<p><m>v(3)=</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1.05409</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\left\lt e^{t-3},0,-3 t^{-2}\right&gt;</m> and at 
<m>t=3</m>
<me>\bf r\it'(3)=\left\lt  e^{3-3},0,-3\cdot 3^{-2} \right&gt; = \left\lt 1,0,-\frac{1}{3}\right&gt;.</me>
The speed is the magnitude of the velocity vector, that is,
<me>v(3)=\|\bf r\it'(3)\|=\sqrt{1^2+0^2+\left(-\frac{1}{3}\right)^2}=\sqrt{\frac{10}{9}}
\approx 1.05</me>


</solution>
